    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "Not sure I fully understand this bump. I think it comes from:\r\n\r\n- https://github.com/lerna/lerna/issues/1569#issuecomment-413376084\r\n- https://github.com/lerna/lerna/issues/2379\r\n- https://github.com/algolia/instantsearch/commit/e5b4fa6ea13be49f526d33bbffe8b8a002b8c334\r\n\r\nIt knows there's a change in Create InstantSearch App as there was a diff, it doesn't know what the version should be, it asks conventional-commits, which says \"level 0\", but as it knew there was a change, it still defaulted to patch.\r\n\r\nBehaviour seems a little overzealous to me, as even if we patch to remove in the release, it will re-add it next time since there was no release yet. \r\n\r\nBest to let it happen I guess, maybe make it so it relies on latest version from the packages anyway, so we don't worry about it needing to update needlessly, when it always updates",
    "commit_id": "1302409838d92d9c70a776c4f29ef6939504869e",
